From 0d6b1f1628834ecadd3767726911af94d1962bf5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Strahinja Stamenkovic <strahinja.stamenkovic@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:28:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix MSVC complex helpers in C-translated LAPACK

The f2c-style headers in lapack-netlib/SRC/*.c carry an `_MSC_VER`
branch (taken by MSVC and clang-cl) with hand-written complex helpers.
Several are wrong and silently corrupt results on Windows:

- zpow_ui multiplied real and imaginary parts element-wise instead of
  doing complex multiplication (and inverted element-wise for n < 0).
  ZLAHQR uses it for its Wilkinson shift, so on real-valued input with
  complex-conjugate eigenvalues the shift collapses, ZLADIV divides by
  zero and ZLAHQR/ZHSEQR/ZGEEV return INFO > 0 with NaN eigenvalues.
  ZHGEQZ (ZGGES/ZGGEV) and ZLAESY use it the same way.
- The inline zdotu_/cdotu_ computed Im = xi*yi + xr*yi instead of
  xi*yr + xr*yi (both stride branches), affecting xLATRS/xLATBS/xLATPS,
  xSPTRI, xSYTRI(_ROOK) and xTRSYL in both precisions.
- The inline cdotc_ strided branch used yi where yr belongs.

Use _Cmulcc/_Cbuild (already used by z_div in the same header) for
zpow_ui, and correct the dot-product imaginary parts. Only files that
call these helpers are changed.

Upstream: https://github.com/OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS/pull/6286
Drop this patch once the OpenBLAS pin includes that change.

Fixes ROCM-34127 (complex128 torch.linalg.eig fails with error code 2
on Windows TheRock PyTorch wheels).
